+// cranvr: BASALT_ACCEPT_MISSING_CONTROLLER=1 is the mode for cranvr-host with a headset whose
+// controllers may sleep. The host gives a game the Touch profile of both hands at its start, also
+// while no controller pose comes, as Unity needs. The left hand may then have the Touch profile
+// with inactive actions, or no profile at all. The program checks the controller's values only
+// while its actions are active, and it waits for no controller. Without the variable the program
+// knows two modes: no profile (no controller), and BASALT_REQUIRE_CONTROLLER_INPUT=1 or the native
+// daemon's injected controller.
+bool acceptMissingController() {
+    const char* value = std::getenv("BASALT_ACCEPT_MISSING_CONTROLLER");
+    return value != nullptr && std::strcmp(value, "1") == 0;
+}
